From: tj-barrett <barrett.t@northeastern.edu>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 21:21:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] LightSpMV: port to *_sync warp intrinsics

__shfl/__shfl_down no longer exist for sm_70+. A blanket full mask would be wrong:
the shuffles sit in row loops that lanes leave at different times. Width-limited shuffles
use the lane mask of the vector (whose lanes share a row); warp-wide row broadcasts in the
loop use the mask of vectors whose row is still in range. A __syncwarp is added after the
lane 0/1 writes to shared memory, which relied on pre-Volta lockstep execution.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
